"""Flutter engine release versions and their metadata.

Each version entry maps a Flutter SDK version string to a struct containing:
- engine_revision: The engine commit hash (used in artifact URLs)
- material_fonts_url: GCS path of the Material icon font bundle
- source_sha256: sha256 of the GitHub source tarball for the release tag

`source_sha256` is **required on every entry**, and read only through
`flutter_source_sha256()` below, so that a missing one is a clear error rather
than an unverified download. Three repository rules fetch the framework source
tarball named by `flutter_source_tarball_url()` in
//flutter/private:artifact_urls.bzl, and all three are pinned against this one
value: `flutter_sdk_package` (once per SDK package in the lock),
`flutter_gen_l10n_repo`, and `flutter_dev_root_repo`.

A mismatch is a loud, intended failure. GitHub's autogenerated tag tarballs
have been re-compressed before, so a break means re-hash the release, not work
around the check. Pinning also lets Bazel's content-addressed repository cache
serve every one of those fetches from a single download; an unpinned fetch can
never be deduplicated that way.

ARTIFACT_CHECKSUMS maps version → artifact_path → sha256.
"""

load("//flutter/private:artifact_urls.bzl", "flutter_source_tarball_url")

